D3D12, validation: a non-array texture view of a layer other than the first is refused.

D3D12's non-array 1D, 2D and 2DMS views and its cube view have no array slice, so
DescriptorD3D12::Create drops TextureViewDesc::layerOffset for TEXTURE, SUBPASS_INPUT,
STORAGE_TEXTURE and TEXTURE_CUBE views of a 1D or 2D texture, and the view addresses the first layer
(or cube) without a word. Vulkan honours it (baseArrayLayer). An array view would not match the
shader's non-array declaration, so D3D12 cannot express such a view. Since 0c5f574 (initial commit).

This refuses it: the D3D12 backend reports it and returns INVALID_ARGUMENT, and NRI validation
refuses it on every backend, pointing to the "_ARRAY" view types, which address any layer on both
backends.
Measured on v190, NVIDIA: a two-layer texture, a STORAGE_TEXTURE view with layerOffset 1,
CmdClearStorage: Vulkan cleared layer 1, D3D12 layer 0, with no message from NRI validation or
either backend's layer. With the change, TEXTURE and STORAGE_TEXTURE views with layerOffset 1 and a
TEXTURE_CUBE view with layerOffset 6 are refused with INVALID_ARGUMENT and one error naming
"layerOffset" and "_ARRAY", on both backends with NRI validation and on D3D12 without it; the same
views of the first layer are created.

diff --git a/Source/D3D12/DescriptorD3D12.hpp b/Source/D3D12/DescriptorD3D12.hpp
index edb17bb9..a257c8ae 100644
--- a/Source/D3D12/DescriptorD3D12.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D12/DescriptorD3D12.hpp
@@ -69,6 +69,13 @@ Result DescriptorD3D12::Create(const TextureViewDesc& textureViewDesc) {
     Dim_t layerNum = textureViewDescFixed.layerNum == REMAINING ? (textureDesc.layerNum - textureViewDescFixed.layerOffset) : textureViewDescFixed.layerNum;
     Dim_t sliceNum = textureViewDescFixed.sliceNum == REMAINING ? (textureDesc.depth - textureViewDescFixed.sliceOffset) : textureViewDescFixed.sliceNum;
 
+    // Non-array 1D and 2D views (and a cube view) have no array slice in D3D12, so they can't select a layer
+    const bool isNonArrayView = textureViewDescFixed.type == TextureView::TEXTURE || textureViewDescFixed.type == TextureView::SUBPASS_INPUT || textureViewDescFixed.type == TextureView::STORAGE_TEXTURE || textureViewDescFixed.type == TextureView::TEXTURE_CUBE;
+    if (textureDesc.type != TextureType::TEXTURE_3D && isNonArrayView && textureViewDescFixed.layerOffset != 0) {
+        NRI_REPORT_ERROR(&m_Device, "'layerOffset=%u' can't be selected by a non-array view in D3D12, use the '_ARRAY' view type", textureViewDescFixed.layerOffset);
+        return Result::INVALID_ARGUMENT;
+    }
+
     m_ViewDesc.texture = {};
     m_ViewDesc.texture.layerOffset = textureViewDescFixed.layerOffset;
     m_ViewDesc.texture.layerNum = layerNum;
diff --git a/Source/Validation/DeviceVal.hpp b/Source/Validation/DeviceVal.hpp
index 5cf190c0..133431a4 100644
--- a/Source/Validation/DeviceVal.hpp
+++ b/Source/Validation/DeviceVal.hpp
@@ -478,6 +478,10 @@ NRI_INLINE Result DeviceVal::CreateDescriptor(const TextureViewDesc& textureView
     NRI_RETURN_ON_FAILURE(this, textureViewDescFixed.layerOffset + layerNum <= textureDesc.layerNum, Result::INVALID_ARGUMENT,
         "'layerOffset=%u' + 'layerNum=%u' must be <= texture 'layerNum=%u'", textureViewDescFixed.layerOffset, layerNum, textureDesc.layerNum);
 
+    bool isNonArrayView = textureViewDescFixed.type == TextureView::TEXTURE || textureViewDescFixed.type == TextureView::SUBPASS_INPUT || textureViewDescFixed.type == TextureView::STORAGE_TEXTURE || textureViewDescFixed.type == TextureView::TEXTURE_CUBE;
+    NRI_RETURN_ON_FAILURE(this, textureDesc.type == TextureType::TEXTURE_3D || !isNonArrayView || textureViewDescFixed.layerOffset == 0, Result::INVALID_ARGUMENT,
+        "'layerOffset=%u' must be 0 for a non-array 'viewType' (D3D12 can't select a layer there), use the '_ARRAY' view type", textureViewDescFixed.layerOffset);
+
     NRI_RETURN_ON_FAILURE(this, textureViewDescFixed.sliceOffset + sliceNum <= textureDesc.depth, Result::INVALID_ARGUMENT,
         "'sliceOffset=%u' + 'sliceNum=%u' must be <= texture 'depth=%u'", textureViewDescFixed.sliceOffset, sliceNum, textureDesc.depth);
 
